{
"what": "a probe of tools/qa/probes.ts by what it does to the game between two ticks (tools/blitz/qa-census.py --kinds, by reading); `tools`: the stand-alone tools, by hand; `pins`: the checks that ran with a settled switch off its page value; `waits`: the checks seen red on the Rust game and green on the TypeScript tick, by hand, each with what it waits on; `families` and `unread`: the other names probes.ts knows",
"tools": {
"tour.ts": {
"word": "ts",
"why": "calls the tick's rules between ticks (kind iii)"
},
"soak.ts": {
"word": "ts",
"why": "calls the tick's rules between ticks and wraps a rule's tick (kind iv-a)"
},
"tools/qa/exact-check.ts": {
"word": "none",
"why": "it holds the game's own maths under bun to the same under node, and node has no bridge preload: a check of the TypeScript tick's arithmetic"
},
"tools/qa/dice-check.ts": {
"word": "none",
"why": "it checks the TypeScript die's own rules (src/math/dice.ts: a game with no die draws Math.random, a die put in Math.random's place is followed), which are the TypeScript tick's and go with it"
},
"tools/qa/playthrough.ts": {
"word": "rust",
"why": "84 of 84 missions end the same under both words"
},
"tools/qa/seats-run.ts": {
"word": "rust",
"why": "its record, replay and twice lines pass under both words"
},
"tools/qa/bench-seeds.ts": {
"word": "rust",
"why": "the same run twice passes under both words on one digest"
},
"tools/blitz/thrice.ts": {
"word": "rust",
"why": "three games of one process are one game, each equal to the TypeScript game on every tick"
},
"tools/blitz/die-check.ts": {
"word": "rust",
"why": "the game's die seeded after the stand lands on the same word under both"
},
"tools/qa/seats-check.ts": {
"word": "ts",
"why": "`rollback` and `twin` hold the game to a word made by walking the JavaScript objects and `down` calls hitPlayer (kinds iv-c, iii): 3 red on the Rust game"
},
"tools/qa/lesson-run.ts": {
"word": "ts",
"why": "a lesson's own checks read records the every-tick list lacks and it hangs its own light meter on the game (kind iv-a)"
},
"tools/mp/server.ts": {
"word": "ts",
"why": "the game server's check runs on the wall clock (a tick every 16.7 ms): with its export and apply a tick of the Rust game is 27 to 45 ms in each of the check's three processes on a loaded box, and its `lag` line counts the records that came late"
},
"tools/mp/bot.ts": {
"word": "ts",
"why": "the game server's check runs on the wall clock (a tick every 16.7 ms): with its export and apply a tick of the Rust game is 27 to 45 ms in each of the check's three processes on a loaded box, and its `lag` line counts the records that came late"
}
},
